    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will this work with my car?",
            "text": "<p>Works with any 2016+ vehicle with factory CarPlay or Android Auto \u2014 that's 500+ models from Toyota, Honda, Ford, BMW, and 30+ brands. Not compatible with Tesla, Rivian, or Lucid.</p><p><a href=\"/pages/supported-cars\">Check your car \u2192</a></p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What's the difference between Elite and Pro?",
            "text": "<p>Both include wireless CarPlay, Android Auto, and full streaming. Elite adds:</p><ul><li><strong>Split-screen:</strong> Navigate and stream simultaneously \u2014 Pro cannot do this</li><li><strong>8GB RAM</strong> vs 2GB in Pro \u2014 4x the processing power, no lag</li><li><strong>64GB storage</strong> vs 16GB in Pro \u2014 more downloaded content, more apps</li><li><strong>Enhanced UI</strong> \u2014 premium interface designed for Elite</li><li><strong>Faster CPU</strong> \u2014 apps open instantly, no waiting</li></ul>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does the split-screen actually work while driving?",
            "text": "<p>Yes \u2014 Elite's split-screen runs live while the car is in motion. You can have Waze directions on one half and a streaming app on the other. Video playback is intended for passengers. The driver should always focus on the road.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do I need WiFi for streaming?",
            "text": "<p>Streaming uses your phone's mobile hotspot \u2014 just turn it on and AutoLinkr connects automatically. Most plans include hotspot data. Many apps also support offline downloads so you can watch without any data connection at all.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is Elite worth the extra $120 over Pro?",
            "text": "<p>If split-screen multitasking, significantly faster performance, or more storage matters to you \u2014 yes. Elite is built for power users who want the absolute best. If you primarily want wireless CarPlay and basic streaming, Pro handles that perfectly.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I move it between cars?",
            "text": "<p>Absolutely. It's completely portable \u2014 unplug from one car's USB port and plug into another. Works instantly in any compatible vehicle.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What if it doesn't work with my car?",
            "text": "<p>30-day money-back guarantee. Return it for full in-store credit. We cover return shipping. No questions asked.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long does shipping take?",
            "text": "<p>Free standard shipping on all orders, 6-10 business days. Most orders placed before 2pm ET ship the same day.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
